times used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Shaw", "streams": 133862, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "ElGrandeToto", "streams": 98197, "best_position": 26}, {"artist": "Najm", "streams": 59366, "best_position": 5}, {"artist": "Inkonnu", "streams": 25150, "best_position": 25}, {"artist": "7liwa", "streams": 7519, "best_position": 93}, {"artist": "7ARI", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "DIZZY DROS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "DRAGANOV", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "jazz": {"genre": "jazz", "country_code": "ma", "country_name": "Morocco", "summary": "Jazz is a musical art form which originated around the beginning of the 20th century in Black communities in the Southern United States from a confluence of African and European music traditions. The style's West African pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Sade", "streams": null, "best_