es of rock music also use keyboard instruments such as organ, piano, mellotron, and synthesizers. Other instruments sometimes utilized in rock include saxophone, harmonica, violin, flute, French horn, banjo, melodica, and timpani. Also, less common stringed instruments such as mandolin and sitar are used. Rock music usually has a strong back beat.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chase Atlantic", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Coldplay", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Evanescence", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lil Peep", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "shoegaze": {"genre": "shoegaze", "country_code": "ma", "country_name": "Morocco", "summary": "Shoegaze is a style of alternative rock  that emerged from the United Kingdom and Ireland in the late 1980s. It lasted until the mid 1990s, peaking circa 1990 to 1993.\n\nThe British music press (notably NME and Melody Maker) called this genre \"shoegazing\" because the musicians in these bands often maintained a motionless performing style, standing on stage and staring down at their effects pedals while playing their instruments (hence, the idea that they were gazing at their shoes).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Beach House", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Cigarettes After Sex", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"art